     "why": "a constrained initial design decides whether the run ever sees a FEASIBLE point, and a run that does not see one rides a box corner for the rest of its budget (optimize.feasible). On the reported 20-D box, 4.7 % of draws fly: 0.5 x dim (10 points) returned NOTHING on 2 of 3 seeds (0/0/12 feasible evaluations of 72) while dim + 1 (21 points) returned a design on 3 of 3 (28/5/31). One case, three seeds -- a rule about the REGIME (a seed smaller than the dimension on a mostly-refused box is blind), not a tuned constant. The V3 shell's screened initial design (bo_feasibility) attacks the same failure from the other side and makes this survivable rather than unnecessary."
    }
